<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Molepolole</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Molepolole is a large village in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, about 50 kilometres north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaborone">Gaborone</a>, and the administrative centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kweneng-district">Kweneng District</a>. It became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakwena">Bakwena</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sechele-i">Sechele I</a> in the 1860s, and missionaries later founded the Scottish Livingstone Hospital there. With a population of over 70,000, it is one of Botswana's largest villages.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/molepolole.jpg" alt="Molepolole" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lerotsi at English Wikipedia · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Molepolole_Shopping_Mall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
